  "body": "## What changed\n\nPer-operation coolant choice.\n\n- Each operation gets a coolant mode: Off / Flood (default) / Mist / Through tool. Flood is what every built-in post already emitted, so existing programs post byte-identical.\n- The motion stream carries it only when it isn't Flood: a `PARAM Coolant off|mist|through-tool` line before the op. Old streams and `.cl` files post as Flood.\n- All six built-in posts take the code from the mounted machine's coolant list (`.mch`), not a hard-coded M7; Heidenhain included. If the machine has no code for the chosen coolant, the post is refused by name (Mist and Through tool; Flood on a machine without a flood code still posts silently - see the follow-up issue). For example, Through tool on the default VMC is refused, and the mill-turn's Through-spindle posts M88.\n- Switching is unchanged: coolant comes on per op, and M9 goes out before each tool change and at program end. An Off op writes neither code.\n- The edit goes through `EditOperationParams::with_coolant` as one undo step. The op stays generated, since coolant doesn't change the toolpath.\n- UI: a Coolant dropdown sits under Tool on the operation page.\n- Project files write `\"coolant\"` only when it isn't Flood; old files load as Flood.\n- Docs: RECOMMENDED.md, assets/posts/AGENTS.md, docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md.\n- About 30 test files that build an op by hand gain `coolant: Default::default()`.\n\n## Readings / pins\n\n- New app `coolant` suite (7): Flood→Mist across the five mill posts gives M8, M9, the tool change, M7, M9. Off writes no codes. Through tool is refused on the default VMC, and a machine with Through-spindle posts M88. Also the project round trip, an old file loading as Flood, and undo/redo.\n- Green: conformance 5 (every golden byte-exact), posting 17, project_roundtrip 68, commands_undo 30, fanuc_post 8, lathe_post 5, lathe_post_refusals 5, machine 32, operations 117, post_engine 31, ui lib 237. Clippy on app, post and ui is clean.\n- Goldens: only the UI snapshots `egui_app.png` / `egui_app_light.png` change, from the new Coolant row. No G-code or CL golden changed.\n\nChangelog: Operations choose their coolant - Off, Flood (default), Mist or Through tool - and every post writes the mounted machine's own code for it, M9 before each tool change and at program end; a coolant the machine has no code for blocks the post by name\n\nFixes #112\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
